#: ../../webgis-src/chb1_mapserver-setup/sec03_hello-mapserver/section.rst:4
msgid "Start using Mapfile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb1_mapserver-setup/sec03_hello-mapserver/section.rst:6
msgid ""
"The core program of MapServer is used to generate maps based on "
"geospatial data. Configure the function of using CGI and give it the "
"function of WebGIS. MapServer uses a configuration file to declare the "
"size and format of the generated map, all paths, names, formats of the "
"data used, and various more complex control options. This configuration "
"file is called Mapfile. Mapfile is multi-layered, and each map file "
"defines a large number of other objects. These objects include scale "
"bars, legends, map colors, map names, map layers, and so on. There are "
"more objects that need to be defined and will be discussed in more detail"
" in the following sections. In addition, there is a comprehensive "
"reference for special MapServer keywords."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb1_mapserver-setup/sec03_hello-mapserver/section.rst:18
msgid ""
"The first application uses a simple Mapfile and does not actually "
"generate a map， it generates a rectangular picture showing the word "
"“Hello World”. This application is very simple, so configuration problems"
" or errors can be easily found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb1_mapserver-setup/sec03_hello-mapserver/section.rst:23
msgid ""
"Each object is explained when it is used. The program does not use any "
"resources, such as spatial data, symbols, fonts and so on. However, it "
"needs space to store images. You will see how to specify the directory of"
" images in MapServer and make sure that Apache can find this directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb1_mapserver-setup/sec03_hello-mapserver/section.rst:30
msgid "Grammar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb1_mapserver-setup/sec03_hello-mapserver/section.rst:32
msgid "MapFile files ignore letter case"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb1_mapserver-setup/sec03_hello-mapserver/section.rst:33
msgid ""
"Non-alphabetic strings or strings containing MapServer keywords must be "
"enclosed in quotation marks. It is recommended that all strings be "
"enclosed in double quotation marks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb1_mapserver-setup/sec03_hello-mapserver/section.rst:36
msgid ""
"File paths in MapFile can use absolute paths or relative paths, where "
"relative paths are relative to ``SHAPEPATH``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb1_mapserver-setup/sec03_hello-mapserver/section.rst:38
msgid ""
"MapFile has a specific hierarchy, Map Object is the “root” of MapFile, "
"and other objects are under it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chb1_mapserver-setup/sec03_hello-mapserver/section.rst:40
msgid ""
"The comment in the MapFile file starts with ``#``, and the part from "
"``#`` to the end of the line is the commented part, and the content of "
"this part will be ignored when the program is executed. Writing notes is "
"a good habit and recommended."
